<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n72897" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὄλβια</span></b> , τά, older
		form for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄλπια,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the Alps,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Posidon.
				48
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i> ; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὄλπια</span></b>  in <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				623.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀλβία</span></b> , ἡ, name of several cities, of which the best known was
			the Milesian colony in Scythia, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				286.15
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv B. C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				7.3.17
			</span></i>, etc. : its citizens being <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀλβιοπολῖται</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				286.1
			</span></i> : hence Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀλβιοπολῑτικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				218.16
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
